Scenario: A historical MAv2 send_message call and an encrypted parent reply reach both Guardian reviews exactly once, in order. Calls retain their original IDs, namespace and encryption metadata, with a paired evidence-only output. The second review appends to the first request. Ciphertext and decisions are mocked; this verifies transport, not backend decryption or authorization outcomes.

## Window 1
